Wait, 210 is listed. $2 > 1$ and $2 > 0$. Correct.
So the condition is simply: Let the digits be $D = [d_k, d_{k-1}, \dots, d_0]$. Then $d_k > \max(d_{k-1}, \dots, d_0)$.

