$x_1 = x_0 + 1$ if $L_1 \le x_0 \le R_1$, else $x_0$.
$x_2 = x_1 + 1$ if $L_2 \le x_1 \le R_2$, else $x_1$.
...
$x_N = x_{N-1} + 1$ if $L_N \le x_{N-1} \le R_N$, else $x_{N-1}$.

Since $x_i \ge x_{i-1}$, the rating is non-decreasing.
The maximum possible increase is $N$.
The constraints are $N \le 2 \times 10^5$, $Q \le 3 \times 10^5$, and the rating values are up to $5 \times 10^5$.
